window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"aatrox","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q rotation plus W comes online — your first real window to layer sweet spots and chunk him when he walks up for on-hit trades."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"An all-in normally goes your way at 6, but Purgatory executes you outright — and it is 120s at rank 1. Track his R before every commit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His window, not yours — the AP spike pushes Purgatory's execute threshold high enough to erase your revive. Fight only when his ult is down."},{"when":"Late","text":"It levels back out: your extended-fight healing matches his burst, so long brawls on your terms become winnable again."}],"wants":{"you":["Chained Q sweet spots","Fights when Purgatory is down","Long trades that feed healing"],"foe":["Poke you into totem range","Hold Purgatory for your low HP","Short burst windows, no brawls"]},"early":"Levels 1-5 are a pure skill lane. Your Q outranges his walk-up poke but the cooldown is long, so never whiff into the wave — Q the spots he must stand on to CS, and answer his Silver Stake on-hit trades with a sweet-spot Q1 into W. Ashen Pursuit (E) is a flat 10s: punish the window after he spends it.","mid":"At 6 the all-in looks yours on paper, but Purgatory executes low targets outright — check his R before every commit. His first-item spike is the most dangerous stage of the lane: keep your HP topped, shove and reset rather than brawling at half health, and fight in the 120s window right after his ult is spent.","late":"Two items on, your sustain catches back up to his burst and the matchup evens. Drag every fight long — the more autos and Q rotations you land, the more you out-heal his damage, and Soul Ignition costs him health up front before it pays back. In fights, knock him up mid-combo to buy your carries time.","whys":["Even at level 1 — your Q outranges his walk-up poke, but its long cooldown means one whiff hands him the trade for free.","Level 2 stays even; neither of you has a hard commit tool yet, so it's all spacing and sweet-spot discipline.","Level 3 is a wash — your Q layering against his on-hit poke; whoever lands their pattern cleaner wins each trade.","Levels 4-5 stay skill-based: everything hinges on landing sweet spots while sidestepping his poke procs.","At 6 it's even — World Ender's heal amp and combat stats normally win you the all-in, but Purgatory can execute you outright, so it comes down to R timing on both sides.","Locke owns the first-item window: his AP spike pushes Purgatory's threshold high enough to execute through your revive. Survive it by fighting only when his R is down and never brawling at half HP.","Post two items it evens out — your sustain in extended fights matches his burst, so drag every duel long and make him regret staying."]});
