window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"aatrox","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"His spike, not yours — your Q chain is short and dodgeable, and he answers every whiff with his Q-E burst while his passive heals off the chip."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"World Ender is your equalizer: 120s of AD, move speed and amplified healing, extended on a takedown — take one full all-in per ult."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Dreaded Return (W, 14s) and Aureate Rush (E) beat your faded post-ult windows. If World Ender is down, refuse the trade."},{"when":"Late","text":"He out-grinds you in raw sidelane duels once World Ender expires — your fights must be short and ult-timed."}],"wants":{"you":["Guaranteed Q sweet spots","All-ins inside World Ender","Teamfights over sidelane duels"],"foe":["Recast Glaive: knockup","Extended trades post-ult","Out-heal you: Glaive and R"]},"early":"Level 1 is a quiet last-hit war — bank it. He spikes at 2 and 3: your Q chain is short, he sidesteps the sweet spots with Aureate Rush (E, 10s) and answers whiffs with The Darkin Glaive, an auto-attack reset that heals him off the chip. Hold Q for sure hits, trade in the 10s after his E, and let 4-5 arrive — your healing off landed Qs finally squares the trades.","mid":"Level 6 is your equalizer: World Ender is 120s of AD, move speed and amplified healing, extended on a takedown — take one full all-in per ult. After his first item his W pull re-engages through your faded post-ult windows, and Grim Deliverance (R, 110s) heals off the damage it deals, so buy Grievous Wounds and shove.","late":"Two-plus items, he out-grinds you in a raw sidelane duel — Q and R both heal him, so anti-heal is mandatory and Aureate Rush's percent-health damage means armour answers little. Keep fights short and ult-timed, bully him off waves, and drag him to teamfights where chained knockups beat his 1v1 stats.","whys":["Level 1 is a neutral last-hit fest — neither combo threatens a kill, so just stack the wave and play patient.","Zaahen takes level 2: your Q chain is short and he can sidestep the sweet spots, then punish with his Q-E burst while his sustain holds the trade.","Level 3 is still his — every missed Q gets answered by Q plus E burst, and his self-heal shrugs off what you do land.","Levels 4-5 even out because your healing off landed Qs finally matches his poke — hit sweet spots and the trades neutralize.","At 6 it's even: World Ender's stat swing cancels whatever lead he built — but it grants no revive; his passive is the one that does.","First item is Zaahen's — his W uptime and re-engage beat your faded post-ult windows; if World Ender is down, do not take the extended trade.","Two-plus items stay his: sustained DPS and self-heal out-grind you once World Ender expires, so make every fight short and ult-timed."]});
