window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"aatrox","b":"masteryi","win":["Aatrox","Aatrox","Aatrox","Aatrox","Skill","Master Yi","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"W plus a full Q rotation gives you your biggest bullying window — he has no answer, so chunk him every single wave."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"World Ender against Highlander is an even coinflip — Highlander is 85s. Commit at full HP."},{"when":"1st item","text":"The tables turn — Wuju true damage starts outpacing your healing. Stop face-tanking and start playing around cooldowns."},{"when":"Late","text":"His resets and true damage own the 1v1. You become the teamfight frontline whose knockups set up his death."}],"wants":{"you":["Deny farm before level 6","W and knockups break the run-down","Grouped fights, not sidelanes"],"foe":["Survive laning phase","Stick to you at first item","Clean late-game duels"]},"early":"You are the lane bully and this phase decides the game. Your Q outranges and out-damages everything he has at 1-2, and by 3 the W plus full Q rotation gives him no safe CS. Meditate is his only sustain and it's a channel — knock him out of it. Deny farm and bank a real lead before 6.","mid":"At 6 World Ender against Highlander is an even coinflip — commit only at full HP with R up; Highlander is just 85s. The moment his first item finishes, Wuju Style true damage outpaces your healing: stop face-tanking, hold W and knockups to break his run-down, and spend your lead on plates.","late":"The 1v1 belongs to him now — Highlander resets and Wuju Style true damage cut straight through your sustain. Don't sidelane into him without a massive lead. Group instead: chained knockups, W drags and World Ender's heal amp turn you into the frontline that lets your team burst him before his resets snowball.","whys":["Aatrox owns level 1 — The Darkin Blade outranges and out-damages his basic attacks, so hit the sweet spot and chunk him for free.","Level 2 is still yours: your Q combo carries genuine kill pressure while he has no kit to trade back with.","Level 3 adds W to a full Q rotation — he has no answer yet, so this is your biggest bullying window of the game.","Through 4-5 you keep out-trading him before his item and defensive tools come online; deny him every scrap of farm now.","At 6 both ultimates spike — World Ender versus Highlander is roughly even, decided by who commits on better cooldowns and health.","Master Yi flips it at first item: Wuju true damage outpaces your healing. Survive by saving W and your knockups to break his run-down instead of face-tanking the DPS race.","Late is his — Highlander resets and true damage shred through your sustain. Refuse clean 1v1s; drag him into teamfights where your chained knockups feed your whole team."]});
